<article class="env-lemma" id="00PV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PV">Lemma <span data-tag="00PV">10.123.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $\varphi : R[x] \to S$ be a ring map. Let $t \in S$. Assume $t$ is integral over $R[x]$. Let $p \in R[x]$, $p = a_0 + a_1x + \ldots + a_ k x^ k$ such that $t \varphi (p) \in \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\varphi )$. Then there exists a $q \in R[x]$ and $n \geq 0$ such that $\varphi (a_ k)^ n t - \varphi (q)$ is integral over $R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $R'$ and $S'$ be the localization of $R$ and $S$ at the element $a_ k$. Let $\varphi ' : R'[x] \to S'$ be the localization of $\varphi $. Let $t' \in S'$ be the image of $t$. Set $p' = p/a_ k \in R'[x]$. Then $t' \varphi '(p') \in \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\varphi ')$ since $t \varphi (p) \in \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(\varphi )$. As $p'$ is monic, by Lemma <a href="/tag/00PT" data-tag="00PT">10.123.2</a> there exists a $q' \in R'[x]$ such that $t' - \varphi '(q')$ is integral over $R'$. We may choose an $n \geq 0$ and an element $q \in R[x]$ such that $a_ k^ n q'$ is the image of $q$. Then $\varphi (a_ k)^ n t - \varphi (q)$ is an element of $S$ whose image in $S'$ is integral over $R'$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0307" data-tag="0307">10.36.11</a> there exists an $m \geq 0$ such that $\varphi (a_ k)^ m(\varphi (a_ k)^ n t - \varphi (q))$ is integral over $R$. Thus $\varphi (a_ k)^{m + n}t - \varphi (a_ k^ m q)$ is integral over $R$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>